WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.167
A forgotten wallet.

00:00:01.177 --> 00:00:02.532
A famous story.

00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:03.846
The famous story:

00:00:03.856 --> 00:00:07.132
in 1949, Frank McNamara finished dinner in

00:00:07.142 --> 00:00:09.667
New York and found his wallet was

00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:11.047
in another suit.

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:13.479
So, the legend goes, he came back

00:00:13.489 --> 00:00:15.914
in February 1950 and paid with a

00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:19.165
small cardboard card and his signature.

00:00:19.265 --> 00:00:21.827
The Diners Club card began with about

00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:24.482
200 members, and had thousands within a

00:00:24.492 --> 00:00:24.974
year.

00:00:25.098 --> 00:00:27.451
So did the forgotten wallet really happen?

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:28.771
Probably not.

00:00:28.781 --> 00:00:32.246
Diners Club's first press
agent, Matty Simmons,

00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:34.496
later said it never happened, and that

00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:36.958
the story was invented to glamorize the

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.031
card.
